<p>A drone strike caused a fire Sunday in an electrical generator outside the inner perimeter of the Barakah Nuclear Power Plant in the Al Dhafra region of Abu Dhabi, UAE authorities said. The Abu Dhabi Media Office said no one was injured, radiation levels remained normal and the plant’s operations were unaffected. The UAE Ministry of Defence said three drones entered the country from the “western border direction,” two were intercepted and one struck the generator; it said an investigation was under way to determine the source of the attack. No one immediately claimed responsibility, and Emirati officials did not publicly assign blame. Efforts to end the U.S.-Israeli war with Iran and restore Gulf shipping remained stalled.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/_hdvna-6-ZMHqa-9Z3NsHHi__Tz1VKfh0uLWm9pRnsnmEAJdox4XZop7da_2kUUdvp4OyjMnpPw2mpVaYvOjDqljjx-Elp2dYULtLA5-y9I6jvCKFYaUkrdQzhdZJt4eSjxrkcsRpeAnFeqtJ7pFbgsy146BfkNJQuj-EmklGaiOYnlLPMmEyhnJDrgr_3SQzTNchWSr0QZcfUsEGQb4FRmn9QsCawSNhKom_R444C3iXiLNL35QFgkQHguBXvXxjcnJZmcDEUphZsO2TQ' alt='A general view of the Barakah Nuclear Power Plant in Abu Dhabi’s western Al Dhafra Region, shown in a 2020 handout image.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Ceasefire context: SCMP and Euronews tied the strike to tensions around the Iran-war ceasefire.</li><li>Hormuz: Aaj News said Iran stepped up attacks on the UAE earlier in May after President Donald Trump announced a naval mission to try to open the Strait of Hormuz.</li><li>Earlier UAE accusations: Aaj News reported that the UAE had previously accused Iran of attacking Emirati energy targets during the conflict.</li></ul><blockquote>Military activity that threatens nuclear safety is unacceptable - Rafael Grossi</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>UAE Ministry of Defence: The ministry said it was investigating the source of the attacks and did not identify a launch site or operator. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/fire-drone-strike-united-arab-emirates-uae-barakah-nuclear-plant/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>International Atomic Energy Agency: The IAEA said the UAE told it that emergency diesel generators were not affected after the strike. (<a href='https://www.jns.org/news/world/drone-strike-hits-uae-nuclear-power-plant'>JNS</a>)</li><li>Abu Dhabi Media Office: The media office said authorities took precautionary measures after responding to the incident. (<a href='https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20260517-fire-breaks-out-near-nuclear-power-plant-in-abu-dhabi-after-drone-strike-officials-say/'>Middle East Monitor</a>)</li><li>BBC News: BBC News reported that the UAE called the strike a “dangerous escalation.” (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cwy27pkj1l1o'>BBC News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/uae-reports-drone-strike-at-nuclear-power-plant-as-iran-war-deadlock-endures'>UAE reports drone strike at nuclear power plant as Iran war deadlock endures</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3353889/drone-targets-uae-nuclear-power-plant-straining-iran-war-ceasefire'>Drone targets UAE nuclear power plant, straining Iran war ceasefire</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/c4b786a6-55d4-4689-b19e-48a48f7946e6'>UAE says drone strike caused fire at nuclear plant</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/a-drone-strike-causes-fire-outside-a-nuclear-power-plant-in-abu-dhabi/article70990120.ece'>Drone strike causes fire outside nuclear power plant in Abu Dhabi</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cwy27pkj1l1o'>UAE reports strike near Abu Dhabi nuclear power plant</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-israel-iran-war-uae-nuclear-power-plant-hit-by-drone-triggers-massive-fire-11508523#publisher=newsstand'>UAE Nuclear Power Plant Hit By Drone, Triggers Massive Fire</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='